# Git Branch Safety

- Do not implement new work directly on `main`.
- Before coding, create or switch to a task branch:
  - `feature/<scope>`
  - `fix/<scope>`
  - `chore/<scope>`
- Keep branches short-lived and focused on one implementation slice.
- Before merge, require:
  - tests passing
  - architecture checks passing (`scripts/architecture/validate_layers.py`, `scripts/architecture/scan_forbidden_imports.py`)
  - checklist/docs updated for changed scope
- Use `git push --force-with-lease` only for intentional local history rewrites and only on branches you own.
- Do not use destructive git commands (`reset --hard`, forced history rewrites) unless explicitly requested by the user.
